# Per-node overrides for the openbao-volume service. The image ships this empty on purpose: a working
# node needs nothing set here.

# The Raft volume's device. Leave unset and the service finds the single attached DigitalOcean volume by
# itself, which is the expected case. Set it only when a node has more than one volume attached and the
# choice of which holds the secret store should not be inferred.
#RAFT_DEVICE="/dev/sda"

# `none` runs the store on the Droplet's own disk, with no attached volume at all.
#
# This is the one way to say that on purpose, and it has to be said: with this unset, a node that cannot
# find exactly one DigitalOcean volume refuses to start, because OpenBao quietly writing its Raft store
# to the boot disk while an attached volume sits empty is the failure a secret store cannot absorb.
#
# What you give up is everything the volume was buying. The store no longer survives the Droplet, so
# replacing a node for an image bump means restoring a snapshot rather than reattaching a disk, and the
# TLS material has to be installed again on each new node. Take Droplet snapshots if you choose this.
#RAFT_DEVICE="none"
